  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThis Afternoon through Thursday: Warm and Dry\n\nMainly zonal flow aloft is forecast for the first few days of this \nnew work week. This pattern will keep afternoon temperatures mild, \nalbeit slightly above average, with forecast highs mainly in the 60s \nbut some locations may reach 70 on any of these days. In fact, the \npotential for highs to reach or exceed 70 degrees starts becoming \nmore favorable by Wednesday with the 19/13z NBM showing around a 30-\n50% chance of reaching the 70 degree mark. Also by Wednesday, H500 \nridging starts to build north over the central CONUS which further \nincreases the confidence in above average temperatures through this \nweek. Dry conditions will continue given this projected upper \nlevel pattern.\n\nFriday into the Weekend: Dry Conditions Likely Continue\n\nThe central axis of the aforementioned ridge should move east over \nthe Upper Midwest on Friday into Saturday, leading to continued dry \nand warm conditions. Weaker troughing across the eastern US along \nwith a deepening, progressive trough across the west should push the \nridge off to the east late this weekend, or at the very least \nsuppress the ridge further south. As this occurs, it may open up the \ndoor to the potential for light precipitation and cooler conditions \nto return. Forecast guidance unsurprisingly has timing differences \namong other differing variables so confidence is low for any \nprecipitation at this point.",
